{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>Also with me HaShem was enraged because of you.</b> This was so that the decree of weeping for generations would be fulfilled among you, as He decreed in saying: ״אִם לֹא כַּאֲשֶׁר דִּבַּרְתֶּם בְּאָזְנַי כֵּן אֶעֱשֶׂה לָכֶם״ (Numbers 14:28). And the speech in His ears in this matter was their saying ״נָשֵׁינוּ וְטַפֵּנוּ יִהְיוּ לָבַז״ (Numbers 14:3). Therefore He related the matter of His death, even though it did not occur until thirty-eight years later, and He announced it in the midst of the words of the Holy One, blessed be He, that were spoken in the second year after their going out from Egypt — when He said ״אִם יִרְאֶה אִישׁ בָּאֲנָשִׁים הָאֵלֶּה״ (Numbers 14:23), and said as well ״וְטַפְּכֶם אֲשֶׁר אֲמַרְתֶּם לָבַז יִהְיֶה״ (Numbers 14:31) — the intention being that the children would ultimately become a spoil, as the Psalmist explained in saying ״וַיִּשָּׂא יָדוֹ לָהֶם לְהַפִּיל אוֹתָם בַּמִּדְבָּר וְגוֹ׳ וּלְזָרוֹתָם בָּאֲרָצוֹת״ (Psalms 106:26–27). So too Ezekiel testified in saying ״וְגַם אֲנִי נָשָׂאתִי אֶת יָדִי לָהֶם בַּמִּדְבָּר לְהָפִיץ אוֹתָם כוּ׳״ (Ezekiel 20:23). And by relating His matter in the midst of the words of the Holy One, blessed be He, He informed them that preventing His entry with them into the land was the cause that the decree decreed upon their children — that they be a spoil for generations — would be fulfilled among them more for evil, and this itself the Psalmist testified in saying ״וַיַּקְצִיפוּ עַל מֵי מְרִיבָה וַיֵּרַע לְמֹשֶׁה בַּעֲבוּרָם וְגוֹ׳ וַיִּחַר אַף ה׳ בְּעַמּוֹ״ (Psalms 106:32–33)."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:20:18.064324941Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}